UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"info","module":4,"title":"Septic Shock: When to Start Steroids","body":"**Persistent vasopressor-dependent septic shock: when to start hydrocortisone**\n\n**Practical dose + duration trigger (SSC 2021):** ongoing norepinephrine or epinephrine at least 0.25 mcg/kg/min for at least 4 hours to maintain target MAP despite resuscitation. Record the current dose and duration of vasopressor dependence. [2]\n\n**Current guideline:** SSC 2026 suggests IV corticosteroids for adults with septic shock. The older dose/time trigger is a practical reference, not a mandatory waiting period or an exclusion rule. Consider the trajectory and other steroid indications; do not delay treatment of suspected adrenal crisis to meet this threshold. [26]\n\n**Vasopressor sequence:** if MAP is not met on escalating norepinephrine alone, [add vasopressin](#/node/sepsis-vp-second). Steroids are adjunctive and do not replace vasopressor escalation. [26]\n\n**[Hydrocortisone](#/drug/hydrocortisone/septic shock)** 50 mg IV q6h OR 200 mg/day continuous infusion [2]\n\n**Evidence:**\n• **ADRENAL trial** (n=3800): Steroids reduce time on vasopressors, ICU LOS, and duration of intubation. No increase in superinfection. [14]\n• **APROCCHSS trial** (n=1241): Hydrocortisone + [Fludrocortisone](#/drug/fludrocortisone/septic shock) 50 mcg PO daily × 7 days reduced 90-day mortality (43% vs 49.1%) [15]\n• Meta-analyses confirm: shorter shock duration, earlier vasopressor weaning. Mortality benefit debated but possible if started early in sickest patients. [14][15]\n\n**Risks:**\n• Hyperglycemia (monitor and treat)\n• Steroid myopathy risk in paralyzed patients\n• No increased superinfection risk (debunked by ADRENAL) [14]\n\n**Taper:** When vasopressors discontinued, taper over 2-3 days (do not stop abruptly).\n\n**Guideline currency:** SSC 2026 suggests IV corticosteroids for adults with septic shock. [26]","citation":[2,14,15,23,26],"next":"sepsis-cardiomyop","treatment":{"firstLine":{"drug":"Hydrocortisone","dose":"50 mg","route":"IV","frequency":"q6h","duration":"until off vasopressors, then taper","notes":"OR 200 mg/day continuous infusion"},"alternative":{"drug":"Fludrocortisone","dose":"50 mcg","route":"PO","frequency":"daily","duration":"7 days","notes":"Add to hydrocortisone per APROCCHSS protocol"},"monitoring":"Monitor glucose. Taper over 2-3 days when vasopressors discontinued."},"summary":"Hydrocortisone 200 mg/day for septic shock; SSC 2021 practical trigger: norepinephrine or epinephrine at least 0.25 mcg/kg/min for at least 4 hours. Not a mandatory cutoff in SSC 2026."}'::jsonb
